  "notes": "South has 3 possible spade losers and a possible loser in hearts if the defenders' hearts break 3-1. Dummy's club suit will provide discards for South's spade losers.\n\nSouth should draw trump before playing on clubs. After cashing the ♥A and ♥K, South must be careful if it turns out one of the defenders started with 3 hearts. In that case, South should concede his heart loser right away. South can win any return and now take his discards on dummy's clubs.\n\nNotice that if South plays clubs before drawing all of the trumps, a defender short in clubs may be able to trump in before South has had a chance to discard all of the spade losers. South would then have no way to avoid losing a spade trick.",
